      "en": "PROLOGUE."
    },
    {
      "la": "CAP. I. Quod ex propriae miseriae et divinae misericordiae consideratione ad orandum Deum incitari debemus.",
      "column": "977b",
      "chunk": 0,
      "en": "CHAP. I. That from the consideration of our own misery and of the divine mercy we ought to be stirred up to pray to God."
    },
    {
      "la": "CAP. II. De tribus speciebus orationis et generibus supplicationis.",
      "column": "979b",
      "chunk": 1,
      "en": "CHAP. II. On the three kinds of prayer, and on the sorts of supplication."
    },
    {
      "la": "CAP. III. Quid postulatio et quid insinuatio.",
      "column": "980d",
      "chunk": 1,
      "en": "CHAP. III. What postulation is, and what intimation."
    },
    {
      "la": "CAP. IV. Cur orantes legimus interdum ea, in quibus nullae petitionis exprimuntur verba.",
      "column": "981d",
      "chunk": 2,
      "en": "CHAP. IV. Why in praying we sometimes read those things in which no words of petition are expressed."
    },
    {
      "la": "CAP. V. Tribus potissimum modis orantium affectus in Deum excitari.",
      "column": "983a",
      "chunk": 2,
      "en": "CHAP. V. That the affection of those who pray is stirred up toward God chiefly in three ways."
    },
    {
      "la": "CAP. VI. Quantum gratus sit Deo fervens orantis affectus.",
      "column": "984a",
      "chunk": 3,
      "en": "CHAP. VI. How pleasing to God is the fervent affection of one who prays."
    },
    {
      "la": "CAP. VII. De diversis affectuum modis, et quibus psalmis quisque adaptetur.",
      "column": "985b",
      "chunk": 3,
      "en": "CHAP. VII. On the diverse modes of the affections, and to what psalms each is fitted."
    },
    {
      "la": "CAP. VIII. Quod in eodem psalmo saepius ab uno affectu in alium fiat transitus.",
      "column": "986b",
      "chunk": 4,
      "en": "CHAP. VIII. That in the same psalm a transition is often made from one affection to another."
    }
